{"id": "EUVD-2026-95208", "enisaUuid": "b82df41c-ca83-3abb-b2dc-c9c9497d1c66", "description": "Poppler 0.42.0 through 26.10.0 contains a stack-based buffer overflow in Decrypt::revision6Hash() that allows attackers controlling the password to overwrite stack memory when opening AESV3/R6 encrypted PDFs. Attackers can supply a password longer than 127 bytes through applications using the libpoppler, libpoppler-glib or C++ API to overflow the K1 and E buffers, crashing the process or corrupting memory.", "datePublished": "2026-10-08T19:51:12", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-14T16:05:29", "baseScore": 8.3, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:P/PR:N/UI:N/VC:N/VI:L/VA:H/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://gitlab.freedesktop.org/poppler/poppler/-/work_items/1814", "https://gitlab.freedesktop.org/poppler/poppler/-/merge_requests/2398", "https://gitlab.freedesktop.org/poppler/poppler/-/blob/poppler-26.10.0/poppler/Decrypt.cc#L1767", "https://gitlab.freedesktop.org/poppler/poppler", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/poppler-0.42.0-through-26.10.0-stack-buffer-overflow-via-decrypt-revision6hash"], "aliases": ["GHSA-939q-g65h-55jw", "CVE-2026-107705"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.33, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "69986f0a-7b91-3205-a91f-792ed7232fd6", "product": {"name": "poppler", "vendor": {"name": "poppler"}}, "product_version": "0.42.0 \u226426.10.0"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "44040eca-bf65-3008-b02f-d5e448428ac4", "vendor": {"name": "Freedesktop"}}], "isExploited": false}